---
import ContactLinks from '../components/ContactLinks.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" type="profile">
  <article class="prose">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>

    <p>
      I am a {site.role} in physics in the {site.affiliation.department} at the{' '}
      <a href={site.affiliation.url}>{site.affiliation.name}</a> in Leipzig, where I started my PhD
      in 2024.
    </p>

    <h2>Research</h2>
    <p>
      I study how pretrained generative and probabilistic models can be reused reliably when the
      prior or the observation process changes. Simulation-based inference and inverse problems are
      my controlled testbeds for questions about adaptation, posterior reliability, and uncertainty.
    </p>
    <p>
      My PhD project is on deep image reconstruction for fast, ultra-high-resolution MRI. It has
      given me hands-on experience with real forward models, acquisition constraints, and large
      experiments on HPC systems.
    </p>

    <h2>A question I keep returning to</h2>
    <p>
      <em>How does evidence become a new abstraction?</em> I am curious how an intelligent system
      notices that its current way of representing a problem is inadequate, seeks evidence that
      discriminates between explanations, and moves to a better model. This is a guiding interest
      rather than a finished line of work.
    </p>

    {/* TODO: once the flagship paper is public, add education, publications and talks from the CV. */}

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      The best way to reach me is by email at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <ContactLinks />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
